{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":33,"timestamp":"2026-07-14T00:58:35.028680769Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8221bfc3-833d-4a73-8872-2b820cfc192a","title":"Evidence-Based Workflow Gates in Crosslink — consolidated findings","description":"Question: \n\nContext: \n\nFindings: \n\n# Evidence-Based Workflow Gates in Crosslink — Consolidated Findings\n\nSource-verified analysis of adding evidence-based workflow gates to Crosslink, consolidated from the design draft, source inspection of crosslink 0.9.0-beta.1, and two independent v2 scoping passes.\n\n## Headline correction\nThe original design was premised on Crosslink currently enforcing signatures (`signing_enforcement: enforced`) over unsigned history, and that most signature/role/trust primitives were missing. **Both are false:**\n- `signing_enforcement` defaults to `audit` (config_registry.rs:108-112). No enforced state exists.\n- **7 of 8 \"gaps\" in the design's §3.1 table already exist in code.** The real work is wiring/activation, not construction.\n\n## What Crosslink already does (verified)\n- Hub-commit signature verification: signing.rs SignatureVerification + sync/trust.rs:427 verify_recent_commits\n- Lock-commit signature verification (display only): sync/trust.rs:458 + dashboard/reader.rs:362\n- Role-aware agent signing: identity.rs:19-25 AgentRole{Driver,Agent}; agent init --role\n- Trust-approver identity: commands/trust.rs:85-90 records approved_by driver fingerprint\n- Bootstrap completion / cutover: sync/bootstrap.rs:55-64 complete_bootstrap on first trust approve (bootstrap.status pending->complete)\n- allowed_signers auto-population: driver/agent keys self-register (comment crosslink-agent:<id>@host)\n- Canonicalization for signing: signing.rs:683-698 sorted key=value\\n (NOT JSON)\n- Clock-skew tolerance: clock_skew.rs:21 SKEW_THRESHOLD_SECS = 60 (git-timestamp witness)\n\n## The three genuine gaps\n1. Enforcement wiring into the local CLI path (HIGH) — signing_enforcement is read only in the server layer; commands/sync.rs, commands/kickoff/run.rs, commands/swarm/* never consult it.\n2. Runtime event-signature verification (HIGH) — verify_event_signature() (events.rs:505-522) is correct but has no non-test caller.\n3. Role->key binding (MEDIUM) — encode role in the allowed_signers principal (role+agent_id@crosslink) rather than adding a struct field.\n\n## Revised GATE verdicts\nSection 1 — Migration & Compatibility:\n- GATE-1.1 Cutover record — DESCOPE (bootstrap.status already covers it)\n- GATE-1.2 Enforcement guard — REFRAME (merge into Phase 1; keep loud warning)\n- GATE-1.3 Backfill/re-signing — DESCOPE (integrity sign-backfill exists)\n- GATE-1.4 Dry-run/warn mode — REFRAME (keep as dry-run enum variant, Phase 1)\n- GATE-1.5 Driver key retrofit — VALID (simplify with --key-dir for CI)\nSection 2 — Valid Evidence per Role:\n- GATE-2.1 Evidence per role — REFRAME (defer fine-grained roles; Driver/Agent covers MVP)\n- GATE-2.2 Non-repudiation — REFRAME (wire verify_event_signature, Phase 2)\n- GATE-2.3 Orchestrator != evidence — VALID (implicit under simplified roles)\n- GATE-2.4 allowed_signers role field — REFRAME (principal encoding instead of struct field)\n\n## Corrected implementation plan\n- Phase 0: TDD BYPASS tests asserting current audit behaviour\n- Phase 1: Plumb signing_enforcement into local sync/kickoff/swarm; add dry-run variant; respect bootstrap.status\n- Phase 2: Wire verify_event_signature() into sync event-replay + kickoff/swarm completion\n- Phase 3: crosslink trust driver-init [--key-dir] + --force guard + override audit log\n- Phase 4: Reconcile bootstrap.status vs cutover.json (descope the latter)\n- Phase 5: crosslink status --audit-violations / --override-audit reporting\nEffort: ~300 LOC enforcement wiring + ~150 LOC event-sig call sites. Not a new VerificationService module.\n\n## Detailed documents\nFull detail, citations, and the original draft live in to-file/crosslink-gates/:\n- updated-evidence-based-gates.md (consolidated overview)\n- gates-verified-facts.md (source-verified facts)\n- gates-issues.md (revised issues with verdicts)\n- evidence-based-gates.md (original draft)\n- server-crash-postmortem.md (unrelated incident log from this session)\n\n## Open question\nFine-grained Builder/Reviewer/Auditor roles may not be needed; Driver/Agent may suffice permanently. Confirm against a real workflow before extending AgentRole.","priority":"low","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLvX7GPUIFGa+qyaQ7IXbogE7p5ZJpkM+gPegz3MUZieSkjJ6TkSxM5vjaUr89fOu0C3yFYuwiR5swn41NMOjQ0="}
